  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">FRACODEP - Improved health and nutritional status of communities affected by HIV and AIDS</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project continues the work of St Francis Community Development Programme (FRACODEP) in contributing to the reduction of HIV transmission and in mitigating the impact of HIV and AIDS among youths, PLHIV and the general community in Seme sub-county in the Archdiocese of Kisumu. Working with the Ministry of Health it aims to:
- Reduce HIV incidence through onsite and mobile HIV Testing and Counselling (HTC) services;
- Strengthen support systems for people living with HIV and at risk of HIV infection, through support groups, enhanced referral services, sensitisation on HIV avoidance, and hygiene promotion;
- Enhance livelihood security through training and support for agricultural income-generating activities;
- Strengthen organisational and staff capacity to effectively and efficiently deliver quality programme management and community services.</narrative>
  </description>
